# This repository is authored on Windows with `core.autocrlf=true` and every
# file below is parsed by a Linux process: kubectl, docker build, pip, sh.
#
# The vault records this exact trap costing an hour once already. A `.stignore`
# pattern was rewritten to CRLF on checkout, so the line reaching the Linux side
# was `/.git\r`, which matched no directory, and it was invisible from Windows
# because Git Bash's grep tolerates a trailing CR while Linux grep does not.
#
# A literal block scalar in deploy/k8s/deployment.yaml carries a `python -c`
# program, so a stray CR would land inside the string the readiness probe runs.
# Pin the line endings rather than hope every consumer is tolerant.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.csv text eol=lf
*.in text eol=lf
*.txt text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
.dockerignore text eol=lf
.trivyignore text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf
.gitignore text eol=lf

# Binary, never touched.
*.gz binary
*.joblib binary
